LazyOS patch over va1erian/xui `crates/xui-core` at the pinned rev 2747818
(issue #339). `tools/xui/build.py` copies the git checkout to
`target/xui-patched/xui-core`, applies this file there and builds with a
`[patch]` onto the copy; the upstream crate is ~350 KB, so it is not vendored.
Drop this file (and the build.py step) once the fix lands upstream and the
pinned rev is bumped.

Button and ToggleButton called `ui.invalidate(id)` on every MouseMove, even
when already hovered, so hovering one cost a full-window composite plus a
damage commit per pixel of pointer motion. Only the Normal -> Hover edge
changes the face; other moves now return early without invalidating.
(Hyperlink already did this at 2747818.)

--- a/src/widget/button.rs
+++ b/src/widget/button.rs
@@ -97,9 +97,12 @@
                     Event::MouseMove { .. } => {
                         // Do not disturb an active press: a pointer that
                         // jitters between press and release must still click.
-                        if state.get() == ButtonState::Normal {
-                            state.set(ButtonState::Hover);
+                        // Only the Normal -> Hover edge changes the face, so
+                        // any other move repaints nothing.
+                        if state.get() != ButtonState::Normal {
+                            return None;
                         }
+                        state.set(ButtonState::Hover);
                     }
                     Event::MouseLeave | Event::CaptureChanged => {
                         if state.get() != ButtonState::Disabled {
